Some instances of SYS III/V sz.c quitting with a core dump have been reported.
The recently posted mod to rbsb.c to set the VQUIT character to -1
didn't fix the problem.

The definitive solution is to ignore the QUIT signal.

Delete the line that has:

		signal(SIGQUIT, bibi);

and add a line with

	signal(SIGQUIT, SIG_IGN);

just outside of the if statement.


